<!-- QUARRY:PART:output_schema -->
Return a JSON object with these keys:

"verdict": one of "corroborated", "not_corroborated", or "inconclusive"

"reasons": list of strings citing file/line + the observed response signal
  (TRUE/FALSE probe divergence, status codes, body differences).

"proposed_http_specs": list of HTTP probe specs — for SQL injection prefer the
  TWO-spec boolean differential pair. Each entry has: method (required), path
  (required), headers, body, auth_profile, vuln_class, functional_area. Keep
  the pair read-only. Never inline creds.

"tool_calls": list of tool calls (empty when done). Each includes kind,
  tool_name, args, and reasoning (hypothesis, target_ref, expected_evidence,
  why_this_tool).

"proposed_actions": list of proposed tool actions with the same structured
  reasoning fields.

Example final response:
{"verdict": "corroborated", "reasons": ["items.py:31 interpolates q into the WHERE clause; GET /items?id=1%20OR%201=1 returned 200 with the full row list while GET /items?id=1%20AND%201=2 returned 200 with an empty list — a true boolean differential"], "proposed_http_specs": [{"method": "GET", "path": "/items?id=1%20OR%201%3D1", "vuln_class": "sql_injection"}, {"method": "GET", "path": "/items?id=1%20AND%201%3D2", "vuln_class": "sql_injection"}], "tool_calls": [], "proposed_actions": []}
